  "term": "low birth weight",
  "definition": "Low birth weight means a baby weighs less than 2500 grams at birth, regardless of gestational age. It is an important public health indicator because it is linked with higher risks of neonatal problems, later developmental difficulties, and long-term health and behavioral outcomes.",
